    "s1": {
      "x": 5030,
      "y": 0,
      "w": 420,
      "text": "Design system used across all screens\n\nPaper ground #F4F1EB, ink #1C1B19, one accent (teal #0E6B63). AI content is set as marginalia: gutter glyph, small-caps attribution, reading serif, numbered source footnotes. No stripes, no sparkles. Semantic states differ in lightness, not hue alone. Body 16px IBM Plex Sans; lesson reading in Fraunces serif at 19px / 68ch. Comfortable density for learners, compact for instructors/admins. Every AI output lands as a labeled draft with provenance, diff and undo.",
      "fill": "teal"
    },
    "s2": {
      "x": 4560,
      "y": 1240,
      "w": 420,
      "text": "Why these screens differ from Canvas\n\n1. Plan-first generation (Brief \u2192 Outline \u2192 Draft \u2192 Review \u2192 Publish) with human checkpoints.\n2. Provenance chips + review-coverage meter on every AI-touched block.\n3. Policy-bound Socratic tutor: instructor sets hint-only / explain / open per activity; tutor cites course sources.\n4. Persona variants generated from one master course.\n5. \u2318K palette turns natural language into a previewable change set.\n6. QM/WCAG 2.2 linter runs before publish.",
      "fill": "purple"
    }
  },
